libdvdread: use an information file's backup when the two differ.

libdvdread falls back to VIDEO_TS.BUP or VTS_nn_0.BUP only when the IFO
fails to parse. An IFO damaged after its header still parses, and its
garbage is used. A disc's IFO and BUP are identical copies, so when they
differ this reads both, once per title set and before the first open
(ifoOpen, ifoOpenVMGI, ifoOpenVTSI), and uses the backup if it has fewer
failed checks.

